 {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and is healthy again.\n\n- **Rollback:** The latest healthy release was v2.3.0. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both marked unhealthy, so I rolled back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production.\n- **Recovery:** After the rollback, the service reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the SEV2 incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found that it had been created as INC-0001, so I did not open a duplicate. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the regions affected.\n\nFollow-up: someone should investigate why v2.3.1 failed before it is re-released.", "type": "text"}]}]}